# Flaky tests: they still run, and every run reports whether they failed or passed, but a failure
# never fails CI (`cargo xtask known-failing`), so one cannot reset the merge queue. One a line:
# `<test> <issue> <date added> [why]`. `<test>` is nextest's `<binary id>::<test name>`, as in
# KNOWN_FAILING_TESTS; the issue is `#N` and is required; the date is YYYY-MM-DD. Sorted. An entry
# older than 14 days fails `cargo xtask lists`: fix the test and delete the line, or decide what
# else to do with it. See "Quarantining a flaky test" in CONTRIBUTING.md.
